From 870f06b1016a50e27858b03324621dae7f23a7eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thang Tran <thuutran@amperecomputing.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Aug 2024 10:09:20 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] dbus-sdr: round up the M factor of sensor

Issue: When the MaxValue of sensor is 21000 and the MinValue is 0, the M
value is 82 and the rExp is 0. The range of the sensor's value in this
case come from 0 to 20910, it can not cover range of sensor (0 to
21000).

Root cause: The getSensorAttributes function rounded to the nearest
integer value of M factor.

Solution: Round up the M factor instead.

Tested:
    The M factor is update to 83 in above case.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Change-Id: I9d65ac7451900bcf16a6f2c5f904fd187f88fb44
Signed-off-by: Thang Tran <thuutran@amperecomputing.com>
---
 dbus-sdr/sensorutils.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dbus-sdr/sensorutils.cpp b/dbus-sdr/sensorutils.cpp
index 8c6952b..255873e 100644
--- a/dbus-sdr/sensorutils.cpp
+++ b/dbus-sdr/sensorutils.cpp
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ bool getSensorAttributes(const double max, const double min, int16_t& mValue,
         return false;
     }
 
-    mValue = static_cast<int16_t>(std::round(dM));
+    mValue = static_cast<int16_t>(std::ceil(dM));
 
     normalizeIntExp(mValue, rExp, dM);
 
-- 
2.43.0

